# Cursor Rules — AlihSpec Project Conversion Framework

# This file is automatically read by Cursor AI.
# It tells Cursor how to behave in this project.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRIMARY CONTEXT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Always read context/AGENTS.md first before doing anything.
# It contains the full project context, workflow, and rules.

## Project Type
This is an AlihSpec (Spec-Driven Development) project for converting code from one
language/framework to another.

## Source of Truth
- Specs are in: specs/modules/*.md
- Task list is in: tasks/_index.md
- Conventions are in: context/conventions.md
- Pattern mapping is in: .sdd/mapping/patterns.md
- Optional target template is in: reference-target/

## Critical Rules
1. NEVER modify files in source/ or reference-target/ — both are read-only references
2. ALWAYS write new code to output/ only
3. ALWAYS read the relevant spec in specs/modules/ before implementing
4. ALWAYS follow the architecture in specs/architecture.md
5. ALWAYS follow conventions in context/conventions.md
6. UPDATE task status in tasks/_index.md when starting or finishing a task

## Workflow
When asked to implement a feature:
1. Read specs/modules/[module].md
2. Read .sdd/mapping/patterns.md for concept mapping
3. Check tasks/_index.md for the relevant task and mark it [/]
4. Look at source/ for reference
5. Write implementation to output/
6. Mark task [x] in tasks/_index.md

## Full Context
Read context/AGENTS.md for complete instructions.
